WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.566 --> 00:00:01.470
(missile booming)

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.480
- [Narrator] For missiles you
can carry on your shoulders,

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.860
to attack drones.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.140
These are some of
Ukraine's smaller weapons

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.360
and they've been effective
at fighting Russia's bigger

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.953
and more powerful arms.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.250
Military strategists
say these lighter tools

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.640
can help an underdog army
become more like a porcupine.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.560
- The porcupine strategy is really

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.510
when a smaller military tries

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.520
to defend itself from a larger military,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.260
which is the attacker.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.460
And it uses lots of smaller weapons.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.410
- [Narrator] This strategy
has inspired Taiwan

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.090
and even its president to rethink

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.110
how to defend itself against a
much larger adversary, China.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.542
Beijing seized Taiwan as
part of its territory.

00:00:39.542 --> 00:00:40.470
(missile booming)

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.540
And as the possibility
of an armed conflict

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.382
around the island has escalated,

00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:45.215
(soldiers shouting)

00:00:45.215 --> 00:00:46.830
Taipei is taking clues from Ukraine

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.530
to prepare to fight China's powerful army.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.510
(pensive music)

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.180
For several decades, Taiwan
has favored expensive gear

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.550
like fighter jets, helicopters and tanks

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.450
to prepare for a possible war with China.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.700
(Wei speaking in foreign language)

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:09.893
- [Narrator] And this threat

00:01:09.893 --> 00:01:11.370
has become heightened
as tensions have soared

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.640
to the highest point over
Taiwan in more than two decades.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.730
After US House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi visited Taipei,

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.010
Beijing began days of military exercises

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.639
that encircled the island.

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:22.472
(rocket whooshing)

00:01:22.472 --> 00:01:24.030
Launching rocket and ballistic missiles

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.930
and sending navy ships
and war planes nearby.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:27.763
(gun shooting)

00:01:27.763 --> 00:01:30.210
Defense analysts say if there
were an actual invasion,

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:33.240
Taiwan alone wouldn't be
able to ward off China

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.620
because its big-ticket weapons

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.800
would be quickly destroyed
by a more powerful arsenal.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.900
And Taiwan has far fewer soliders compared

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.630
with its neighbor, which has
the world's largest military

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.220
by active personnel.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.660
Given the disadvantages

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.840
that's where the so-called
porcupine capabilities come in.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:49.860
- Much like the animal,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.670
it tries to inflict so much
pain on the larger rival

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.689
that it stops the attacker.

00:01:55.689 --> 00:01:56.850
(gun booming)

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.190
- [Narrator] And one way
to inflict a lot of pain,

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.310
these handheld anti-tank and
anti-aircraft equipment used

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.020
by individual soldiers.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.670
Since the start of the war in Ukraine,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.530
the US has sent thousands of stinger

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.530
and javelin missiles to the battlefield.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.363
(weapon booming)

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.300
And these weapons are particularly useful

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.800
for smaller militaries

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.930
because they're able to
have an outsized impact

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:16.950
on their rival.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.420
- The Russians have been using lots

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.080
of large invasion forces using tanks,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.520
and planes, and the Ukrainians

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.750
have been able to fight back

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.060
by using these smaller weapons

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.980
and using them very effectively

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.080
to destroy large targets.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.760
- [Narrator] So far,
hundreds of Russian tanks

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.110
and aircraft have been destroyed

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.060
since the war broke out in February,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.740
according to an open source website

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.170
that tracks military equipment losses.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.570
And that success has driven
some Taiwanese leaders,

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.880
including the president
to embrace these types

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.730
of anti-tank and anti-aircraft weapons.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.660
Earlier this year,

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.850
Taiwan's legislature
also approved a motion

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.200
to conduct more training,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.000
possibly involving portable missiles

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.160
like the javelin and stinger.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.170
But those handheld
missiles have limitations

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.000
because they only have an operating range

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.326
of about 2.5 miles.

00:03:02.326 --> 00:03:03.570
(missile booming)

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.190
That's why Taiwan, like Ukraine,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.990
is also getting longer-range weapons

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:10.140
like these mobile rocket
launchers called HIMARS.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.550
In Ukraine, they've allowed the army

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.470
to reach beyond Russia's frontline,

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.740
sending missiles up to 53 miles away.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.960
In 2020, the US approved the first sale

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.250
of the weapon to Taiwan

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.470
and the island's Defense
Ministry said it's looking

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.397
to buy more of them.

00:03:24.397 --> 00:03:25.230
(drone whirring)

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.670
Another relatively small weapon

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.520
that can impose heavy
losses from very far away,

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.127
the attack drone.

00:03:31.127 --> 00:03:33.030
- So attack drones can be very useful

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.200
for smaller militaries

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.440
because it enables them
to do significant damage

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.210
behind enemy lines.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.880
Ukrainians have been
destroying Russian tanks,

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.730
convoys that have been
coming into the country.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.410
- [Narrator] The attack drones
have also been effective

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.910
at hitting Russia's navy.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.530
In May, Ukraine released footage

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.080
of what it said were drones
hitting two Russian vessels

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.310
in the Black Sea.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.844
Russia didn't comment
on the Ukrainian claim.

00:03:55.844 --> 00:03:56.677
(weapon booming)

00:03:56.677 --> 00:03:57.720
This type of sea-based assault

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.120
could happen in Taiwan
since military experts say

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.280
a Chinese invasion would involve a lot

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.800
of ships coming over the Taiwan Strait.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.410
So the island has been developing
its own indigenous drones

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.640
like this one.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.884
The US has also agreed to sell some drones

00:04:10.884 --> 00:04:12.990
and Taiwanese lawmakers have been pushing

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.880
to purchase four of them.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.954
- Fire, fire, fire.

00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:16.787
(weapon shooting)

00:04:16.787 --> 00:04:17.620
- [Narrator] Taiwan's government

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.112
isn't just preparing weapons.

00:04:19.112 --> 00:04:20.190
(guns clicking)

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.650
Its citizens are also taking action.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.750
So some people are picking
up shooting lessons,

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.400
just like the Ukrainians,

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.260
and rallying this type of public support

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.372
is also an important part
of the porcupine strategy.

00:04:31.372 --> 00:04:32.205
(guns shooting)

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.600
- In Ukraine, things didn't go as quickly

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.180
as the Russians thought they would.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:39.180
One of the reasons for
that is the motivation

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.630
and the willingness of
the Ukrainian population

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:46.860
to take up arms and to
defend their country.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.020
- [Narrator] So to prepare
its citizens for a war,

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.120
Taiwan's Defense Ministry
is debating plans

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.061
to extend military
conscription for up to a year.

00:04:54.061 --> 00:04:58.440
(Chiu speaking in foreign language)

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.490
- [Narrator] And a survey found

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.170
that more than 70% of adults

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.423
are in favor of a longer service time.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.050
While Taiwan can learn a lot
from Ukraine's experience,

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.730
there are unique challenges.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.200
Ukraine borders other countries

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.310
and that makes it possible

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.830
for its troops to continue
receiving a steady flow

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.330
of weapons and supplies.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.013
- But Taiwan is an island

00:05:18.013 --> 00:05:20.066
and there may be difficulties

00:05:20.066 --> 00:05:23.070
if there is a Chinese invasion for Taiwan

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.190
to receive weapons from other countries,

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.720
particularly if the Chinese form

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.490
a blockade around the island.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:32.100
So it needs to have large stockpiles ready

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.450
for a conflict.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:34.500
- [Narrator] So building that stock

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.000
has become a priority.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.350
This year, the government pledged

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:40.860
any extra $8.7 billion
for military equipment.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.710
The US, which has promised
to help Taiwan defend itself

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.740
has been selling military
gear to Taipei for decades

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.420
and after Pelosi's visit there,

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.610
she said America wouldn't
abandon its commitment

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:51.780
to the island.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.295
- We've worked together
for the security of Taiwan.

00:05:55.295 --> 00:05:59.545
(Hua speaking in foreign language)

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:01.800
- [Narrator] China's
National Defense Ministry

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.720
didn't respond to a request for comment

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.553
about Taiwan's military build-up.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.730
But Taiwan isn't the only
one keeping a close eye

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.110
on the war in Ukraine.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:13.320
Military experts say
China is taking notes too.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.420
- [Alastair] And one of those
would be that if you are going

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:18.570
to try and take over
one of your neighbors,

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:21.327
you need to use overwhelming force.

00:06:21.327 --> 00:06:22.560
- [Narrator] And that's been showcased

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.090
during its live fire drills,

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:27.180
showing its ability to
effectively blockade Taiwan.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:30.000
- [Alastair] If Taiwan is faced with one

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.300
of the world's most powerful
conventional militaries coming

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.590
at you with everything,

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.650
that's a very difficult challenge.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.088
(pensive music)

